      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Before settlers, the Capote band of the Southern Ute tribe used the surrounding San Juan Mountains for hunting and seasonal migration.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/South_Fork,_Colorado",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town’s economy shifted from timber and mining to tourism, with recent decades seeing tourism surpass forestry and mining in employment.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
